  <name>SayItErmano</name>
  <summary>Local voice dictation with AI polish</summary>
  <description>
    <p>Press a key, speak, and polished text lands in any application.
      SayItErmano is a local-first dictation app for Linux: the speech
      model runs on your machine, transcription works offline after the
      first model download, and the app collects no telemetry.</p>
    <p>Dictation uses whisper models (CPU int8 by default; GPU
      acceleration through Vulkan where available). An optional AI
      polish step can clean up the verbatim transcript — with any
      OpenAI-compatible endpoint you configure, or fully offline with a
      bundled local model.</p>
    <p>Works on X11 and on Wayland sessions (GNOME 48+, KDE Plasma,
      Hyprland): the dictation hotkey binds through the desktop
      portals, so no global keyboard grab is needed. A command mode
      lets single utterances steer formatting, languages, and system
      actions.</p>
  </description>
